Z||000000||Cooter||05-31-2000||08:43 PM||||I am getting close to starting my "new" engine/tranny combo and need to know what kind of oil to put in the tranny-'84 model four speed.<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||06-01-2000||08:37 AM||||?||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||06-01-2000||10:51 AM||||did you rebuild (replace bearins seals etc) in the tranny?.. I just did that in my car (4:10 4spd) and put CRAPPY 80-90w gear lube in it for 30 minutes on the dyno running throught the gears. then drained it and refilled it with Amsoil Synthetic 75-90w and drove it home...  If you didn't replace any bearings then you shouldn't have to worry about crap in the case like i had to. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero Mike||06-01-2000||11:06 AM||||Yikes!! Don't use anything other than 5W30 in you 1984 4.10 tranny!!  This is what the factory manual requires.  I know that my tranny had a horrible 3-4 shift grind.  Thinking it was the synchros, I got worried. Turns out that there was gear oil (80W90) in the tranny which made it VERY hard for the synchros to synchronize the shifts (oil was too thick).  I've use 5W30 ever since and NO PROBLEMS.||||reg||13
